WEBVTT

00:10.500 --> 00:13.170
Tsukishima, Chuo City, Tokyo.

00:14.130 --> 00:18.710
Spanning more than 400 years
since the Edo Period, is Takamimi Shrine.

00:16.750 --> 00:19.210
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

00:20.130 --> 00:24.960
The goddess summoned
from another world enshrined here...

00:25.540 --> 00:28.420
was an absolute social recluse of an elf.

00:30.420 --> 00:33.500
Let's spend a day following that elf.

00:38.330 --> 00:41.880
At 7am, the elf's morning starts early.

00:43.380 --> 00:46.000
Elda! It's morning, Elda!

00:46.460 --> 00:50.540
I'm heading to school already!
Make sure you actually get up!

00:51.210 --> 00:55.960
Okay! I'm up!

01:00.210 --> 01:05.500
At 10am, the elf's morning... starts early.

01:05.710 --> 01:06.460
What?!

01:16.380 --> 01:22.250
The elf eats breakfast while on her computer.
She is sensitive to social situations.

01:22.540 --> 01:25.580
Oh, Amazen is having a lightning deal...

01:28.500 --> 01:32.580
Oh, yeah... I wonder if there's a new issue
of some manga coming out.

01:34.080 --> 01:36.580
The new volume of Elf Warriors is coming out!

01:34.080 --> 01:37.080
<b>ELF WARRIORS</b>

01:37.330 --> 01:42.960
I forgot to check for it! B-but if I get
the ebook version, I can read it right away!

01:43.460 --> 01:46.420
B-but I bought a physical copy of the first volume!

01:46.420 --> 01:49.420
I can use rush delivery
and get it delivered tomorrow, though...

01:49.580 --> 01:53.920
<b>Price:</b>

01:49.580 --> 01:53.920
<b>Buy now with 1-Click</b>

01:49.960 --> 01:53.210
The elf, unable to control herself,
has purchased the electronic version!

01:54.460 --> 01:57.210
In the end, she also buys a physical copy.

02:03.500 --> 02:04.460
Hot, hot, hot...

02:05.920 --> 02:07.710
Noon. Lunch.

02:09.000 --> 02:13.960
The elf indulges in the rice ball
and the tomato-simmered mackerel prepared by Koyuzu.

02:15.790 --> 02:19.290
By the way, the rice ball has her favorite filling, tsukudani.

02:24.630 --> 02:28.920
Ah, so that's it. Tama from the Murai Flower Shop is here.

02:43.960 --> 02:46.250
He is always so cute!

02:46.710 --> 02:49.630
Now then, to continue with my meal...

02:50.330 --> 02:53.960
The elf loves animals, but fears touching them.

02:56.670 --> 03:05.750
Any kind of dirt is not unclean if it is not left to stagnate...

02:57.000 --> 02:58.080
5 in the afternoon.

02:58.580 --> 03:03.000
The elf performs her rituals in earnest
since the miko has returned home.

03:05.750 --> 03:07.250
Pull it together!

03:08.750 --> 03:11.000
6 in the evening, dinner.

03:11.880 --> 03:16.330
The elf partakes in a cheese-stuffed hamburger steak
with demi-glace sauce prepared by Koyuzu.

03:17.750 --> 03:18.790
Want some more?

03:19.130 --> 03:20.130
Yes!

03:21.040 --> 03:22.290
8 in the evening.

03:23.420 --> 03:26.750
The elf is a recluse,
but she also plays competitive games online.

03:27.130 --> 03:30.630
O-okay! I will improve my gaming technique
this time, for sure!

03:31.630 --> 03:36.040
Y-you little... ugh! Take that!
And that! And that... and that!

03:42.750 --> 03:46.420
When the elf loses in her game,
she gets rather depressed.

03:47.920 --> 03:49.210
10 in the evening.

03:50.170 --> 03:55.170
The elf is hungry, so she eats dorayaki
that was given as an offering from a parishioner.

03:57.250 --> 04:01.000
It's so popular at the Abara Shop
you can rarely purchase one.

04:01.000 --> 04:02.580
G'night, El... Hey!

04:02.580 --> 04:04.080
You're snacking again?!

04:04.080 --> 04:06.750
W-well, I, uh...

04:07.540 --> 04:09.750
K-Koito, do you want some, too?

04:09.750 --> 04:10.580
Yes I do.

04:15.420 --> 04:18.130
2 in the morning. She emerges from the bath.

04:31.170 --> 04:34.880
There's nothing like a nice,
cold drink after a long hard day of work!

04:36.330 --> 04:40.460
Even if the elf did not work particularly hard,
she has a nice, cold drink.

04:42.130 --> 04:43.330
4 in the morning.

04:46.630 --> 04:48.830
Afterwards, the elf goes to sleep.

04:50.290 --> 04:53.080
As she wishes for a peaceful, unchanging tomorrow...

04:55.580 --> 05:00.830
The goddess is in her Tsukishima;
All is right with the world.

05:02.790 --> 05:05.750
Looking back at it, this is a pretty awful way to live.

06:38.130 --> 06:42.830
<b>EPISODE 10</b>

06:38.130 --> 06:42.830
<b>THE ELVES</b>

06:38.130 --> 06:42.830
<b>AND MIKO</b>

06:38.130 --> 06:42.830
<b>OF 3 CITIES</b>

06:43.960 --> 06:47.210
Making a sacred bow sure is a tough job.

06:51.580 --> 06:53.920
Elda, I got a message from Hima-chan!

06:55.250 --> 07:00.710
<b>Even though parishioners are comin',</b>

06:55.250 --> 07:00.710
<b>Yolde's run away again.</b>

06:55.250 --> 07:00.710
<b>I'm gonna find her and smack her!</b>

06:55.630 --> 07:00.670
"Even though parishioners are comin', Yolde's run
away again. I'm gonna find her and smack her!"

07:01.080 --> 07:02.080
...is what she said.

07:02.460 --> 07:04.540
Poor Hima-chan.

07:05.040 --> 07:09.500
Goodness, that Yolde.
She's just as hopeless as she's always been.

07:10.710 --> 07:12.130
They're gonna get me!

07:12.130 --> 07:16.460
G-go... you little... hya! Take that!

07:16.710 --> 07:20.500
"It seems like one day she's going
to rise in revolt of the Miko Union."

07:32.460 --> 07:35.830
I reckon I told ya that ya can't go
to downtown Umeda by yerself.

07:36.130 --> 07:40.830
It's a downright dungeon over there,
and your sense o' direction is awful.

07:41.080 --> 07:45.750
But I was cravin' some o' that grilled squid!
I even got some for ya!

07:45.880 --> 07:48.920
I don' want it. I wanna drink an Aquarius.

07:49.210 --> 07:51.750
Why not? It's mighty tasty!

07:52.130 --> 07:55.580
You should focus on the parishioners
waitin' for ya instead. Eat it up fast.

07:55.580 --> 07:56.380
'Kay!

07:56.960 --> 08:00.460
Much obliged for today, Hiromimi-san.

08:00.670 --> 08:02.670
Come 'n see me again, Kayo-chan!

08:03.380 --> 08:05.460
I apologize for keepin' ya waitin'.

08:08.540 --> 08:13.330
Good work today. There's nothin' left for ya to do,
so feel free to go on out and play.

08:13.330 --> 08:17.080
Right! But I think I wanna stay home for today.

08:17.080 --> 08:19.750
That's different. You're actin' like Elda-sama.

08:19.880 --> 08:25.750
Well, I haven't been payin' you much attention recently!
Thought I'd stay and play with you today, Hima!

08:26.000 --> 08:29.630
I wanted to do my homework but... I suppose it's fine.

08:30.130 --> 08:31.670
Glad to hear it.

08:32.250 --> 08:34.830
Okay, what do ya wanna play?

08:34.830 --> 08:37.750
Actually, not that anythin' can be done about it now,

08:37.750 --> 08:40.210
but I printed the photos we took
when we were in Tokyo at a convenience store.

08:40.210 --> 08:42.670
For real?! I wanna see, I wanna see, show me!

08:43.750 --> 08:47.540
Tokyo was a hoot, huh? I wanna go again.

08:47.710 --> 08:51.380
Sure was. But next time we gotta make sure
we let 'em know.

08:51.920 --> 08:54.830
Since we went spur o' the moment,
we scared Elda-sama.

08:54.830 --> 08:58.420
We don't need to let 'em know!
They'll meet with us cuz we're cute!

08:58.420 --> 09:01.210
We can't do that. Where'd that confidence come from?

09:01.540 --> 09:04.540
From me! I'm Yolde, ya know!

09:05.580 --> 09:07.630
Oh, this here's Monja Street.

09:08.580 --> 09:11.630
I wanna eat monja in Tsukishima next time!

09:12.000 --> 09:14.580
We couldn't get any before since we were short on time.

09:15.080 --> 09:20.330
I thought it was kinda like a close relative of okonomiyaki,
but seems it's got a different type of deliciousness.

09:20.000 --> 09:21.210
<b>DIFFERENT THING</b>

09:21.580 --> 09:24.880
Ya think Tokyo folk eat monja on the daily?

09:24.880 --> 09:26.210
There ain't no way they do.

09:26.210 --> 09:29.830
Even though yer Osakan, ya don't eat takoyaki every day.

09:30.750 --> 09:32.710
We don't eat it every day!

09:32.710 --> 09:34.670
Right? It's a harmful rumor.

09:35.420 --> 09:38.170
When was the last time we even had takoyaki?

09:38.460 --> 09:41.290
Lemme see... Yesterday. As a snack.

09:42.000 --> 09:44.580
I kinda wanna eat some takoyaki now.

09:44.790 --> 09:47.750
Yeah, me, too. Wanna make takoyaki for dinner then?

09:47.750 --> 09:50.420
We can't! Then we'd be eatin' it every day.

09:53.960 --> 09:58.460
Ya know, there ain't hardly any people
usin' Osaka dialect in Tokyo, huh?

09:58.830 --> 10:02.920
That's true. Learnin' the standard dialect
might turn out better for us.

10:03.250 --> 10:06.380
Yeah! Let's do some standard dialect talkin' right now!

10:06.380 --> 10:08.670
Alrighty. You start us off, Yolde.

10:08.920 --> 10:11.210
"Mighty fine weather we're havin' today,"
try sayin' that one.

10:11.880 --> 10:14.830
T-today... is... mighty fine weather.

10:14.830 --> 10:16.080
Ya can't use "mighty."

10:16.540 --> 10:21.420
Uh, nice weather... I reckon?

10:21.330 --> 10:21.880
<b>I reckon</b>

10:21.540 --> 10:22.500
You "reckon"?

10:25.580 --> 10:28.000
Hog rolls, hog rolls!

10:28.000 --> 10:31.540
Why're you hungry? Ya just had grilled squid.
Hog rolls, hog rolls! Hog rolls!<b></b>

10:31.790 --> 10:34.420
'Cuz there's always room for hog rolls!

10:34.880 --> 10:39.750
Oh? You only got the one hog roll
from the parishioners so eat half.

10:40.290 --> 10:43.830
It's from Haranishi-san, on 3rd street.
You gotta thank her later.

10:44.040 --> 10:47.920
That's Michiko's granddaughter, yeah?
I'll go see her tomorrow!

10:50.830 --> 10:52.790
It's hog roll time!

10:55.290 --> 10:58.080
It's hot! I gotta split it in half!

10:58.080 --> 10:59.080
Careful now.

10:59.540 --> 11:00.790
Hot! Hot!

11:13.250 --> 11:17.750
I... I'm the older sister 'round here,
so I'm givin' the bigger half to you, Hima!

11:22.790 --> 11:27.130
I'm more in the mood for red bean buns today.
You eat the big half.

11:29.420 --> 11:32.540
Alright! If that's what you want, guess I gotta!

11:32.540 --> 11:34.420
Yep, thanks.

11:34.630 --> 11:36.630
Time to chow down!

11:44.040 --> 11:46.580
Me and this older sister sure are funny.

11:47.080 --> 11:49.080
Hm? Whatcha say?

11:49.290 --> 11:51.880
Nothin'. Don't let it get cold now.

11:52.000 --> 11:54.880
'Kay! Hog rolls sure are tasty!

11:55.210 --> 11:58.960
<b>TOMORROW IS</b>

11:55.210 --> 11:58.960
<b>ANOTHER DAY!</b>

11:55.210 --> 11:58.960
<b>HIROMIMI SHRINE</b>

11:55.880 --> 11:58.080
Tomorrow is another day!

12:01.830 --> 12:06.210
<b>Kanazawa City - Ishikawa Prefecture</b>

12:11.000 --> 12:13.000
That's... Isuzu-chan, isn't it?!

12:13.000 --> 12:15.710
It's really her! She was on TV the other day!

12:15.710 --> 12:17.290
Isuzu-chan!

12:21.460 --> 12:23.960
She's so sparkly!

12:24.710 --> 12:26.500
I am Isuzu Koimari.

12:26.880 --> 12:30.460
As an influencer, my days are very fulfilling to me.

12:30.920 --> 12:35.880
<b>URAMIMI SHRINE</b>

12:32.290 --> 12:35.880
As things are, my prime concern right now, is...

12:35.880 --> 12:43.330
<b>Sparkle</b>

12:35.880 --> 12:43.330
<b>Sparkle</b>

12:35.880 --> 12:43.330
<b>Sparkle</b>

12:35.880 --> 12:43.330
<b>Sparkle</b>

12:36.880 --> 12:40.170
the handmade photobooks of Haira
that I started making when I was ten,

12:40.170 --> 12:42.830
and how I was closing in
on my next one becoming the 200th.

12:46.830 --> 12:50.500
I've gotten much more skilled at using my camera,
and for the next one...

12:50.500 --> 12:56.000
<b>HAIRA</b>

12:50.500 --> 12:56.000
<b>HAIRA</b>

12:50.500 --> 12:56.000
<b>HAIRA</b>

12:50.500 --> 12:56.000
<b>HAIRA</b>

12:50.500 --> 12:56.000
<b>HAIRA</b>

12:51.040 --> 12:54.500
I want to make a photobook that can be called
a compilation of everything up until now!

12:55.380 --> 13:00.250
I gotta take a super sparkly photo of Haira
that's worthy of being the cover!

13:01.630 --> 13:03.130
I'm home, Haira.

13:03.290 --> 13:05.710
Oh my, Isuzu, welcome back.

13:07.290 --> 13:09.380
Oh, are you taking a picture?

13:09.710 --> 13:13.330
I don't mind, but is it all right if I borrow your bicycle?

13:16.630 --> 13:17.330
No.

13:17.330 --> 13:19.210
Wh-why not?!

13:19.380 --> 13:21.080
Where are you going by bicycle?

13:21.080 --> 13:26.960
U-um, well... I thought I'd take up cycling for my health...

13:26.960 --> 13:28.880
You're going to the boat racing venue, aren't you?

13:31.290 --> 13:37.420
As a miko, an enshrined deity going to a boat racing
venue 20 kilometers away by bike is a no-go.

13:37.460 --> 13:41.920
<b>Maybe the Horse Races</b>

13:37.460 --> 13:41.920
<b>Maybe the Boat Races</b>

13:37.460 --> 13:41.920
<b>It's Uramimi-sama</b>

13:37.750 --> 13:39.290
You heard the rumors from just the other day

13:39.290 --> 13:41.670
of you standing to pedal and roaring down
the national highway, right?

13:42.170 --> 13:45.420
I thought I'd be late to the race
I was aiming to see so I was pedaling like crazy!

13:45.420 --> 13:49.710
Didn't I tell you that you've more or less
already used up this month's allowance?

13:50.790 --> 13:51.750
About that...

13:51.960 --> 13:54.960
With the scratch ticket that I bought yesterday
with the measly 200 yen I had,

13:55.290 --> 13:57.830
I got a lucky break and made bank with just one ticket!

13:57.830 --> 14:00.670
I'll use this as seed money
and rake in the dough at the boat races!

14:02.380 --> 14:03.130
Oh, yeah.

14:03.380 --> 14:06.710
You still haven't paid me back the 3,000 yen
you borrowed, have you?

14:06.710 --> 14:09.710
Huh? Is that so?

14:10.130 --> 14:13.960
I'm positive you said "You can even charge me
10% interest every 10 days, just let me borrow it!" Right?

14:13.960 --> 14:16.290
Eh?! D-did I?!

14:16.580 --> 14:19.040
You got a lucky break, right?

14:22.210 --> 14:25.790
You did indeed. Interest is considered a loss.

14:26.210 --> 14:29.420
I'm flat broke before I've even left for the boat races...

14:34.710 --> 14:41.080
I'm flat broke, so I'll do some gardening.
Would you like to help me out, Isuzu?

14:41.460 --> 14:44.170
Sure. I like your garden.

14:45.000 --> 14:49.130
Besides, if we're here,
I think I can get some sparkling photos of you.

14:52.880 --> 14:57.500
You sure have a lot of plants in your garden, Haira.
What's this one called?

14:57.960 --> 14:59.580
It is a scented Solomon's seal.

15:00.080 --> 15:02.420
There's a sweetness to the young buds
and the underground stem,

15:01.580 --> 15:02.750
<b>Solomon's seal</b>

15:02.420 --> 15:05.130
so if you make it into tempura
or a veggie dish with dressing it's quite delicious.

15:05.750 --> 15:06.580
And this?

15:06.790 --> 15:11.500
Giant Butterbur. Simmered dishes, tsukudani,
and sautees are delicious when made with those.

15:08.380 --> 15:09.290
<b>Giant Butterbur</b>

15:12.000 --> 15:12.880
And this one?

15:12.960 --> 15:19.290
Purslane. It goes well in salad, but it's delicious
when made into namul with sesame and garlic.

15:15.130 --> 15:16.080
<b>Purslane</b>

15:19.920 --> 15:22.080
Do you only have edible wild herbs?

15:22.330 --> 15:26.380
My goodness, you were eating them
and kept calling them delicious yesterday, weren't you?

15:26.580 --> 15:28.420
You ate the shepherd's purse
in the sesame dressing dish.

15:28.630 --> 15:31.380
Seriously?! That was sheperd's purse?!

15:31.630 --> 15:36.420
Yes. It's also known as, Nazuna.
It's one of the spring herbs.

15:37.250 --> 15:39.960
All of the spring herbs are hardy plants,

15:37.460 --> 15:42.710
<b> JAPANESE PARSLEY</b>

15:38.250 --> 15:42.710
<b>NAZUNA</b>

15:39.000 --> 15:42.710
<b>JERSEY CUDWEED</b>

15:39.750 --> 15:42.710
<b>CHICKWEED</b>

15:40.210 --> 15:42.540
so it's easy to obtain them even in cold winters.

15:40.500 --> 15:42.710
<b>HENBIT</b>

15:41.250 --> 15:42.710
<b>TURNIP</b>

15:42.000 --> 15:42.710
<b>WHITE RADDISH</b>

15:43.000 --> 15:46.130
It has been an important source of nutrition
since the old days.

15:46.580 --> 15:50.500
Wow. When I think of sheperd's purse, I imagine...

15:51.380 --> 15:56.540
the gift you brought to the Takamimi Shrine
that grew on the side of the road.

15:56.540 --> 16:02.080
Sh-shall we have some tea?!
Look, we can relax with the mint I picked!

16:07.670 --> 16:11.040
I didn't get a single shot, much less a sparkling Haira.

16:11.750 --> 16:13.790
Isuzu, what are you looking at?

16:13.790 --> 16:19.540
Huh? Oh, check this out, it's a monsterous raddish
that a reporter picked at a farm they went to.

16:19.710 --> 16:22.790
My, it looks like the thigh of a pro cyclist!

16:23.080 --> 16:25.880
You don't have to mention
those sorts of things all the time.

16:28.170 --> 16:28.880
What?

16:29.290 --> 16:35.750
Isuzu, ever since you became an... influencer, is it?
You look like you've really been enjoying yourself.

16:36.210 --> 16:39.920
Uh... Well, yeah. It's fun.

16:40.630 --> 16:43.710
Since I'm the enshrined deity of Kanazawa,

16:44.040 --> 16:48.920
I've been a little jealous of you
flitting around the world like a little bird.

16:50.000 --> 16:53.380
It's not like you have to
just stay in Kanazawa forever, though.

16:54.000 --> 16:59.630
Yolde-sama at Hiromimi Shrine says she does
a whole lot of traveling. And by the way...

17:01.630 --> 17:05.500
I'll take you anywhere you want to go.

17:07.250 --> 17:08.540
Isuzu...

17:10.040 --> 17:12.040
Okay then, I want to go to Las Vegas!

17:12.040 --> 17:13.290
Absolutely not.

17:13.290 --> 17:16.380
Oh, really? But it looks so fun...

17:18.170 --> 17:21.830
Well, I don't care if I can't go anywhere.

17:23.330 --> 17:27.580
If I'm with you, Isuzu, I enjoy wherever I am.

17:31.170 --> 17:31.790
Hey!

17:31.790 --> 17:34.500
Whoa! You can't just grab other people's phones...

17:35.830 --> 17:37.420
I hope that was a cute shot of us!

17:37.790 --> 17:42.710
Uh, the layout is a mess, and it's out of focus.

17:44.460 --> 17:45.040
But...

17:46.580 --> 17:49.540
<b>ISUZU URAMIMI HIME-NO-MIKOTO</b>

17:46.580 --> 17:49.540
<b>SPARKLE</b>

17:46.590 --> 17:49.540
<b>THIS ONE'S AN ULTRA RARE!</b>

17:46.590 --> 17:49.540
<b>LET'S HANG OUT AGAIN.</b>

17:46.590 --> 17:49.540
<b>-ISUZU</b>

17:46.590 --> 17:49.540
<b>SPECIAL ANNIVERSARY ISSUE</b>

17:49.540 --> 17:53.040
<b>ISUZU URAMIMI HIME-NO-MIKOTO</b>

17:49.540 --> 17:53.040
<b>SPARKLE</b>

17:53.330 --> 17:56.500
She said this is Haira-sama's 200th photobook.

17:56.500 --> 17:59.330
Th-the cover is such a nice picture, right?

17:59.500 --> 18:03.710
Yeah, they seem to be as close as they always are,
Isuzu and Haira-sama!

18:04.580 --> 18:07.170
Well, I don't want a photobook, though.

18:07.290 --> 18:09.130
Yeah... neither do I.

18:10.210 --> 18:14.000
<b>WORSHIP</b>

18:10.210 --> 18:14.000
<b>DEAD OR ALIVE</b>

18:10.210 --> 18:14.000
<b>URAMIMI SHRINE</b>

18:10.420 --> 18:12.500
DEAD OR ALIVE!

19:58.710 --> 20:00.540
<b>Alarm</b>

19:58.710 --> 20:00.540
<b>Snooze</b>

19:58.710 --> 20:00.540
<b>Stop</b>

20:09.540 --> 20:10.330
Okay.

20:11.000 --> 20:14.710
5:20 in the morning. The miko's morning starts early.

20:16.670 --> 20:21.250
The first thing that happens every day,
is making an offering to her deity.

20:29.750 --> 20:34.210
Elda, it's morning. I'm leaving you a Red Bull, m'kay?

20:35.630 --> 20:37.580
5:30 in the morning.

20:38.460 --> 20:43.380
Cleaning of the entrance
and grounds occurs every day, without fail.

20:44.000 --> 20:50.420
The miko's mind, which keeps the grounds beautiful,
is now in a state of clarity.

20:50.420 --> 20:52.500
<b>RUUUUUUMBLE</b>

20:53.130 --> 20:54.830
Or perhaps not...

20:56.290 --> 20:58.080
I wonder what's for breakfast.

20:59.130 --> 21:00.500
6 in the morning.

21:00.670 --> 21:03.040
She partakes of the breakfast made by Koyuzu.

21:04.170 --> 21:08.880
Then, at 7, she calls out to the deity
before leaving for school.

21:09.380 --> 21:12.420
Elda! It's morning, Elda!

21:12.880 --> 21:16.960
I'm heading to school now! Make sure you wake up!

21:17.670 --> 21:22.210
Okay! I'm up!

21:24.170 --> 21:25.130
She's asleep.

21:27.540 --> 21:28.420
Noon.

21:29.500 --> 21:32.540
In the daytime, the miko devotes herself to her studies.

21:35.580 --> 21:39.380
Koma-chan, Koma-chan, aren't these heels amazing?

21:39.380 --> 21:40.670
I don't think they suit you.

21:41.670 --> 21:43.290
If these were blue, then may-

21:43.290 --> 21:44.040
They don't suit you.

21:46.920 --> 21:48.080
3 in the afternoon.

21:48.750 --> 21:51.830
Studies are over,
and she takes a brief break with her friend.

21:53.040 --> 21:55.580
Oh, it's Tama, from Murai Flower Shop.

21:55.580 --> 21:58.080
Can't believe how beautiful you are right meow!

21:59.380 --> 22:00.210
Tama!

22:00.630 --> 22:02.080
Let us pet you!

22:02.420 --> 22:05.380
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

22:03.000 --> 22:07.420
4 in the afternoon. Soon after returning home,
she enters the amulet office.

22:08.500 --> 22:11.330
Writing the shrine's seal stamp
is also the duty of the miko.

22:12.170 --> 22:15.330
Then, putting all her heart and soul
into the worshippers who come for a visit...

22:17.790 --> 22:19.750
Welcome, thank you for visiting us today.

22:20.460 --> 22:22.920
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

22:20.710 --> 22:27.380
Any kind of dirt is not unclean if it is not left to stagnate...

22:21.420 --> 22:22.460
5 in the afternoon.

22:23.130 --> 22:26.170
She recites the shinto prayers
to Takamimi-no-Mikoto Hime.

22:27.790 --> 22:29.250
Pull it together!

22:32.170 --> 22:34.540
8 in the evening. She emerges from the bath.

22:40.880 --> 22:45.670
She drinks one liter of milk everyday, in the hopes
of becoming the adult woman she aims to be.

22:47.500 --> 22:52.960
<b>FUTABA</b>

22:47.500 --> 22:52.960
<b>CHOICE</b>

22:47.500 --> 22:52.960
<b>FUTABA MILK</b>

22:48.750 --> 22:52.670
She has not grown taller as of yet,
but she is extremely healthy.

22:53.580 --> 22:54.710
10 at night.

22:57.290 --> 23:02.130
She offers thanks to the
Takamimi-no-Mikoto Hime and pays her respects.

23:03.750 --> 23:07.500
It's so popular at the Abara Shop
you can rarely purchase one.

23:07.500 --> 23:10.710
G'night, El... Ah! You're snacking again?!

23:10.880 --> 23:13.380
W-well, I, uh...

23:14.170 --> 23:16.210
K-Koito, do you want some, too?

23:16.380 --> 23:17.250
Yes I do.

23:18.920 --> 23:20.830
10:30 at night.

23:21.580 --> 23:24.960
The miko stays up a little late, and she chats with the elf.

23:25.630 --> 23:31.290
And you know, this afternoon the Murai Flower Shop's
cat, Tama was in the yard, and he was very cute!

23:31.500 --> 23:36.250
Yeah, I saw him, too, around 3rd street.
Cats are cute, right?

23:36.420 --> 23:38.750
Tama is especially cute.

23:38.750 --> 23:41.960
Yeah, the most beautiful cat in Tsukishima!

23:50.630 --> 23:52.170
11 at night.

23:54.040 --> 23:56.130
The miko falls asleep.

23:56.580 --> 23:58.880
While wishing for a better tomorrow...

24:00.000 --> 24:04.880
The goddess sits in Tsukishima,
and there is only peace upon the Earth.

24:09.250 --> 24:12.960
<b>WORSHIP</b>

24:09.250 --> 24:12.960
<b>DON'T WORRY ABOUT</b>

24:09.250 --> 24:12.960
<b>THE DAY TO DAY</b>

24:09.250 --> 24:12.960
<b>TAKAMIMI SHRINE</b>

24:10.210 --> 24:12.540
Don't worry a-about the day to day!
